---
import BlogPostLayout from '../../../../layouts/BlogPostLayout.astro';

const title = "The 10 core life skills by WHO: examples and how to practise each in India";
const seoTitle = "The 10 Core Life Skills by WHO: Examples and How to Practise Each";
const description = "The 10 core life skills by WHO with simple examples for students in India, five pairs to practise, free activities and how each helps a career.";
const seoDescription = "The 10 core life skills by WHO with examples, five pairs to practise and free activities for students in India.";
const canonical = "https://futurecareerschool.com/blog/skills/10-core-life-skills-by-who-examples-and-practice-india/";
const publishedDateISO = "2026-10-30";
const publishedDateLabel = "30 October 2026";
const authorName = "Shivanshi Sehgal";
const authorUrl = "https://futurecareerschool.com/about/shivanshi-sehgal/";
const authorRole = "Career researcher and writer";

const faqItems = [
  {
    "q": "What are the 10 core life skills by WHO?",
    "a": "Self-awareness, empathy, critical thinking, creative thinking, decision making, problem solving, effective communication, interpersonal relationship skills, coping with stress and coping with emotions."
  },
  {
    "q": "Which organisation listed the 10 core life skills?",
    "a": "The World Health Organization. Check the current wording on its official site."
  },
  {
    "q": "How do I teach these skills?",
    "a": "Use short activities, such as role plays and decision cases, then discuss what happened."
  },
  {
    "q": "How do life skills differ from soft skills?",
    "a": "They overlap, but life skills also cover self-care and coping."
  },
  {
    "q": "Why do life skills matter for a career?",
    "a": "They decide how you decide, communicate and handle pressure at work."
  },
  {
    "q": "How do I practise empathy?",
    "a": "Listen without interrupting and repeat back what you heard."
  },
  {
    "q": "Where do I start?",
    "a": "Choose one pair and practise it for two weeks."
  },
  {
    "q": "What if I feel overwhelmed?",
    "a": "Talk to a trusted adult, a teacher or a qualified professional."
  }
];

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faqItems.map((item) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: item.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: item.a },
  })),
};
---

<BlogPostLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  seoTitle={seoTitle}
  seoDescription={seoDescription}
  canonical={canonical}
  category="skills"
  publishedAt={publishedDateISO}
  publishedLabel={publishedDateLabel}
  authorName={authorName}
  authorUrl={authorUrl}
  authorRole={authorRole}
  jsonLdExtras={[faqJsonLd]}
>
  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>The World Health Organization lists ten core life skills: self-awareness, empathy, critical thinking, creative thinking, decision making, problem solving, effective communication, interpersonal relationship skills, coping with stress and coping with emotions.</strong> The decisions that unlock high income opportunities are practising one pair at a time and building a high-income skill portfolio with steady habits, because AI can explain the list but cannot practise it for you.
  </p>

  <div class="key-takeaways">
    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Short answer:</strong> ten skills in five pairs, practised one pair at a time.</li>
      <li><strong>Evidence:</strong> your own weekly practice notes. We quote no statistics.</li>
      <li><strong>Growth:</strong> pairing these skills with one earning skill in a small service has the most headroom, and it is the base of an earlier path to financial freedom.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p>
    This guide is part of our set of <a href="/blog/skills/">skills and career-building guides</a>. Read it with <a href="/blog/skills/best-skills-for-high-salary-in-india/">best skills for high salary in India</a>, <a href="/blog/skills/how-to-find-which-skills-are-in-demand-in-india/">how to find which skills are in demand</a> and <a href="/blog/skills/how-to-learn-a-new-skill-and-prove-it-india/">how to learn a new skill and prove it</a>.
  </p>

  <nav class="jump-nav" aria-label="Article sections">
    <p class="jump-nav__label">Jump to section</p>
    <ul class="jump-nav__list">
      <li><a href="#verdict">The verdict</a></li>
      <li><a href="#evidence">What the data shows</a></li>
      <li><a href="#routes">Routes</a></li>
      <li><a href="#sales">Who pays you</a></li>
      <li><a href="#ai">AI and disruption</a></li>
      <li><a href="#better">Better alternatives</a></li>
      <li><a href="#learn">Learn it cheaply</a></li>
      <li><a href="#activities">Simple activities for each</a></li>
      <li><a href="#money">Money</a></li>
      <li><a href="#checkpoint">The 4-Checkpoint Protocol</a></li>
      <li><a href="#gate3">The 3 Gates</a></li>
      <li><a href="#mistakes">Expensive mistakes</a></li>
      <li><a href="#next-step">What to do next</a></li>
      <li><a href="#faq">FAQs</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <h2 id="verdict">The short answer: ten skills in five pairs, practised one pair at a time</h2>

  <p>
    The World Health Organization lists ten core life skills for young people: self-awareness, empathy, critical thinking, creative thinking, decision making, problem solving, effective communication, interpersonal relationship skills, coping with stress and coping with emotions. They are often taught in pairs.
  </p>
  <p>
    Schools and colleges use this list for life skills education, and it appears in many exam questions. For a career, the useful step is to practise one pair at a time and keep a short note of what changed.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Skill pair</th>
          <th>What it means</th>
          <th>How to practise</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Skill pair"><strong>Self-awareness and empathy</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it means">Know yourself and understand others</td>
          <td data-label="How to practise">Write three strengths and three triggers, then ask a friend what they notice.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Skill pair"><strong>Critical thinking and creative thinking</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it means">Check claims and generate options</td>
          <td data-label="How to practise">Question one news claim a week and list five ways to solve one problem.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Skill pair"><strong>Decision making and problem solving</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it means">Choose and fix</td>
          <td data-label="How to practise">Write pros, cons and a review date for one real choice.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Skill pair"><strong>Effective communication and interpersonal relationships</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it means">Speak, listen and build trust</td>
          <td data-label="How to practise">Hold one difficult conversation calmly and note what helped.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Skill pair"><strong>Coping with stress and coping with emotions</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it means">Stay steady and recover</td>
          <td data-label="How to practise">Try a regular sleep, movement and break routine and record how you feel.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="evidence">How to use the list, and what to verify</h2>

  <p>
    The ten skills come from WHO life skills education guidance. Check the current wording on the official WHO and education board sites, because school syllabi may phrase them slightly differently.
  </p>
  <p>
    For a career, pair each skill with a real task, such as running a meeting for communication or tracking a budget for decision making.
  </p>
  <p>
    We quote no statistics. Your own practice notes are the evidence. Our <a href="/blog/skills/what-are-life-skills-examples-and-how-to-build-them-india/">life skills guide</a> gives a monthly plan.
  </p>
  <p class="note-line">
    This page does not quote statistics. The method is the evidence: your own practice notes, one pair at a time.
  </p>
  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      If stress or low mood is affecting daily life, talk to a trusted adult, a teacher or a qualified professional. Self-help habits are not a substitute.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="routes">Six ways to use these skills, strongest growth first</h2>

  <div class="route-grid">
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">01</span>
        <span class="chip chip--high">Scalable</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Pair the skills with one earning skill and a small service</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">Clear communication, decisions and steady habits keep clients and cash steady.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Clients.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>Repeat customers and references.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Cash flow and scope need care.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Add services and help.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">02</span>
        <span class="chip chip--mid">Scalable with a business layer</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Interview and placement preparation</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">Self-awareness and communication show quickly.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Employers.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>Mock interview improvements.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Skills still need domain proof.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Add a work sample.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">03</span>
        <span class="chip chip--mid">Scalable with a business layer</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Peer mentoring and club leadership</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">Practise empathy and communication with real people.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Colleges.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>Feedback from peers.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Titles alone prove little.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Lead a small project.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">04</span>
        <span class="chip chip--mid">Scalable with a business layer</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Teaching and facilitation</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">Teaching life skills builds your own.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Schools and NGOs.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>A workshop you ran.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Needs preparation.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Move toward training roles.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">05</span>
        <span class="chip chip--low">Not so scalable</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Memorising the list for exams only</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">Knowing the names is not practice.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Exams only.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>Marks.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Habits need repetition.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Practise one pair a month.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">06</span>
        <span class="chip chip--low">Not so scalable</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Trying all ten at once</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">Overloaded plans fade.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Nothing.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>None.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Start small.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Pick one pair.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>The ownership path:</strong> run a small workshop for juniors on one skill pair, such as decision making and problem solving, with a simple activity and feedback form.
    </p>
    <p>
      Keep the plan and the feedback as proof of facilitation.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="sales">Who rewards these skills, and how they notice</h2>

  <p>
    Teachers, employers and clients notice calm, clear and fair people. They see it in how you decide, speak, listen and handle pressure.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic habit is a weekly note: one skill, one situation and one thing you will do differently.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and life skills</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools can explain these skills and suggest activities. This raises the value of practising them with real people.
  </p>
  <p>
    Prefer practice over reading: use AI for ideas, then try them in a real situation. A staged path helps: now, use AI for prompts and reminders; later, handle the conversations and decisions that need your judgment.
  </p>

  <h2 id="better">Common mix-ups to avoid</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Alternative</th>
          <th>Why it can beat it</th>
          <th>Catch</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Alternative"><strong>Treating life skills as theory</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Why it can beat it">Marks do not build habits.</td>
          <td data-label="Catch">Practise in daily situations.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Alternative"><strong>Mixing up soft skills and life skills</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Why it can beat it">They overlap, but life skills also cover health and coping.</td>
          <td data-label="Catch">Use both lists.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Alternative"><strong>Ignoring stress signs</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Why it can beat it">Ignoring them can make things worse.</td>
          <td data-label="Catch">Talk to a trusted adult or professional if needed.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="learn">How to practise each skill free, and what proof counts</h2>

  <p>
    Skill is learned by doing real work, so the cheapest route is also the best. A paid course is worth it only when it gives feedback and finished work that you cannot get free.
  </p>
  <h3>Free and low-cost routes first</h3>
  <ul class="check-list">
    <li>Free NPTEL and SWAYAM lessons in communication and management.</li>
    <li>Official WHO and education board pages for definitions.</li>
    <li>Free YouTube talks on stress and study habits.</li>
    <li>A notebook for weekly notes.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>How to judge a paid course</h3>
  <p>
    Judge each course, not the platform. Ask what you will build, who reviews it, which role graduates reached, how current the material is and what the refund terms are, in writing.
  </p>
  <h3>Your week, and a first small test</h3>
  <p>
    A starting plan is about ten hours a week: three of lessons and seven of practice on one project. Do not pay for an expensive programme before this habit holds.
  </p>
  <p>
    In ten weeks, practise one pair every two weeks, write a weekly note and ask a friend to give feedback.
  </p>
  <h3>Building a high-income skill portfolio beside the credential</h3>
  <p>
    A degree has a place, and the weak spot is relying on it alone. A skill mix of one core skill, a second skill, communication, a niche and a clear offer builds a high-income skill portfolio, and a niche service can bring an earlier financial freedom.
  </p>

  <h2 id="activities">Simple activities for each pair</h2>

  <p>
    Try one activity per pair. Each takes under thirty minutes and needs no equipment.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Pair</th>
          <th>Activity</th>
          <th>What to note</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Pair"><strong>Self-awareness and empathy</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Activity">Write your strengths, then listen to a friend for five minutes without advice</td>
          <td data-label="What to note">What surprised you</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Pair"><strong>Critical and creative thinking</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Activity">Test one claim from social media and list five uses for a common object</td>
          <td data-label="What to note">What evidence you found</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Pair"><strong>Decision making and problem solving</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Activity">Plan a small trip budget with two options</td>
          <td data-label="What to note">What you chose and why</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Pair"><strong>Communication and relationships</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Activity">Hold a short, honest conversation about a small disagreement</td>
          <td data-label="What to note">What helped</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Pair"><strong>Coping with stress and emotions</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Activity">Keep a sleep and break routine for a week</td>
          <td data-label="What to note">How you felt each day</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Repeat the activity a month later and compare your notes.
  </p>

  <h2 id="money">Money: course fees and the 10 percent test</h2>

  <p>
    As a rule of thumb and not a research finding, keep a degree or course fee near a tenth of the family's total education budget, and treat spending above roughly a fifth as a serious caution that needs course-specific evidence.
  </p>
  <p>
    An illustration, not a real fee: on a Rs 5 lakh education budget, a tenth is Rs 50,000 for the main course, and a fifth is Rs 1 lakh as a serious caution. The rest can fund a laptop, practice time and a reserve.
  </p>
  <p>
    Test the field with free courses and one finished project before paying for a long programme. Do not borrow heavily for a course whose graduates cannot show placement in a specific role.
  </p>

  <h2 id="checkpoint">The 4-Checkpoint Protocol for this skill</h2>

  <p>
    Test the choice with <strong>The 4-Checkpoint Protocol</strong>: Biology, Context, Market and Survival.
  </p>
  <div class="protocol">
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">01</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Biology: can you do this kind of work for years?</div>
        <p>Do one small real task and notice whether the daily work suits you.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">02</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Context: time, money and home support</div>
        <p>Count the months to a portfolio, the cost and how you will live meanwhile.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">03</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Market: who pays for your skill?</div>
        <p>Read ten live notices for the role you want and note the skills they ask for.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">04</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Survival: what survives AI?</div>
        <p>Routine tasks shrink first. Build judgment, checking skill and a niche.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="gate3">The 3 Gates: proof before commitment</h2>

  <p>
    <strong>The 3 Gates</strong> check that your effort turns into work other people rely on.
  </p>
  <div class="gates-block">
    <div class="gates-row">
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Gate 1</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Proof of skill</span>
        <p>Finish one real project in your chosen specialty.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Gate 2</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Proof you can explain it</span>
        <p>Show it to a working professional and fix what they flag.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Gate 3</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Proof someone will pay</span>
        <p>Land one paid task, internship or written reference.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="mistakes">Expensive mistakes</h2>

  <div class="mistake-list">
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">01</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Paying for a long course first</div>
        <p>Test with free material and one finished project before paying.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">02</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Choosing the label over a skill</div>
        <p>Pick one core skill and prove it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">03</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Skipping the live notices</div>
        <p>Employers tell you what they pay for, so read them.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">04</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Relying on one employer or client</div>
        <p>Build a second route and an owned list.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">05</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Treating a certificate as proof</div>
        <p>A finished project and a reference prove skill.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>

  <p>
    Pick one route, finish one project and show it to two people in the field. Then read ten live notices and apply or pitch a small client.
  </p>
  <p>
    A specialist can look at your strengths, finances and goals with you. A sensible first step is <a href="/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/student-career-guidance/">student career guidance</a>. The aim is a high-income skill portfolio and an earlier path to financial freedom.
  </p>

  <p>
    For a checklist before joining a programme, read <a href="/blog/skills/skill-india-nsdc-and-government-skill-programmes-india/">Skill India and NSDC programmes</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    For a weekly review you can show, read <a href="/blog/skills/self-management-skills-examples-and-how-to-build-them-india/">self-management skills</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    For a four-move listening practice, read <a href="/blog/skills/interpersonal-skills-and-active-listening-india/">interpersonal skills and active listening</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    For five skills with five small projects, read <a href="/blog/skills/21st-century-skills-examples-for-students-india/">21st century skills</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    For five skills and small practices for shy people, read <a href="/blog/skills/empathy-and-social-skills-examples-and-how-to-build-them-india/">empathy and social skills</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    For everyday habits and when to ask for help, read <a href="/blog/skills/stress-and-coping-skills-for-students-and-freshers-india/">stress and coping skills for students and freshers</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="faq">FAQs on the 10 core life skills by WHO</h2>

  <div class="faq-accordion">
    {faqItems.map((item, index) => (
      <details open={index === 0}>
        <summary>{item.q}</summary>
        <div class="faq-a">{item.a}</div>
      </details>
    ))}
  </div>

  <style>
    .check-list { display: grid; gap: 0.55rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; margin: 0.5rem 0 1.25rem; line-height: 1.7; }
    .lead-para {
      font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 1.65vw, 1.2rem);
      line-height: 1.85;
      color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82) !important;
      margin-top: 0 !important;
    }
    .lead-para strong { color: #fff; }

    .jump-nav {
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.09);
      border-radius: 16px;
